From: Librescoot
Subject: [PATCH] fill-extrusion: use a position-only program for the depth prepass

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]

Worth upstreaming in principle, but it adds a program to a generated-shader
scheme that upstream has since replaced wholesale in the drawables renderer,
so it would not apply there.

Translucent fill-extrusion layers are drawn twice: once into the depth buffer
with the colour mask off, then again for colour with a stencil test. The
prepass exists so that on a footprint that self-overlaps in projection only
the nearest surface gets blended.

Both passes used the same program, so the depth pass ran the full lighting
vertex shader (relative luminance, a dot product, two mixes, a pow, three
clamps, ~42 instructions) and then discarded every bit of it but gl_Position.

The buildings layer is vertex-shader bound on the DBC (i.MX6DL, Vivante GC880:
one shader core, one pixel pipe), so that waste is most of the prepass.
Confirmed vertex bound rather than fill bound by scaling fill-extrusion-height
to 5%, which keeps the vertex count and cuts fill area roughly twentyfold: no
change (13.3 to 13.6 fps, inside noise).

This adds a second program sharing FillExtrusionProgram's attributes, uniforms
and paint properties, so the layer feeds it identical bindings, and differing
only in GLSL: it computes the same gl_Position and nothing else. Measured on
the DBC map screen:

  stock                       12.7 fps, 60.6 ms in swap
  position-only depth pass    15.1 fps, 47.4 ms in swap

The algorithm is unchanged, so the output is too: captured the same frozen
view with each library and compared. Across the 172800 pixels of the map
region, zero differ.

For contrast, dropping the prepass altogether reaches 18.4 fps but produces
visible back-face artifacts on self-overlapping footprints (7.2% of pixels
differ by more than 5%), so it is not an option.

diff --git a/vendor/maplibre-native/include/mbgl/shaders/gl/fill_extrusion_depth.hpp b/vendor/maplibre-native/include/mbgl/shaders/gl/fill_extrusion_depth.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..86a3b5819e5a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/maplibre-native/include/mbgl/shaders/gl/fill_extrusion_depth.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+// Position-only variant of FillExtrusionProgram, for the depth prepass.
+// Hand written: the sibling fill_extrusion.hpp is generated, this is not.
+
+#pragma once
+#include <mbgl/shaders/shader_source.hpp>
+
+namespace mbgl {
+namespace shaders {
+
+template <>
+struct ShaderSource<BuiltIn::FillExtrusionDepthProgram, gfx::Backend::Type::OpenGL> {
+    static constexpr const char* vertex = R"(uniform mat4 u_matrix;
+
+attribute vec2 a_pos;
+attribute vec4 a_normal_ed;
+
+#ifndef HAS_UNIFORM_u_base
+uniform lowp float u_base_t;
+attribute highp vec2 a_base;
+#else
+uniform highp float u_base;
+#endif
+#ifndef HAS_UNIFORM_u_height
+uniform lowp float u_height_t;
+attribute highp vec2 a_height;
+#else
+uniform highp float u_height;
+#endif
+
+void main() {
+    #ifndef HAS_UNIFORM_u_base
+highp float base = unpack_mix_vec2(a_base, u_base_t);
+#else
+highp float base = u_base;
+#endif
+    #ifndef HAS_UNIFORM_u_height
+highp float height = unpack_mix_vec2(a_height, u_height_t);
+#else
+highp float height = u_height;
+#endif
+
+    vec3 normal = a_normal_ed.xyz;
+
+    base = max(0.0, base);
+    height = max(0.0, height);
+
+    float t = mod(normal.x, 2.0);
+
+    gl_Position = u_matrix * vec4(a_pos, t > 0.0 ? height : base, 1);
+}
+)";
+    static constexpr const char* fragment = R"(void main() {
+    gl_FragColor = vec4(1.0);
+}
+)";
+};
+
+} // namespace shaders
+} // namespace mbgl
